WEBVTT

00:56.250 --> 00:57.458
Hayden?

01:02.250 --> 01:03.416
Who's this?

01:06.166 --> 01:07.708
He's my son.

01:10.750 --> 01:11.958
He's a Payne.

01:14.791 --> 01:16.250
What have you done?

01:53.333 --> 01:54.541
Hey, buddy, what are you doing?

01:55.458 --> 01:56.625
Dad!

01:57.250 --> 01:58.582
Hey. Come on.

01:58.583 --> 02:00.083
Oh!

02:02.083 --> 02:05.999
Do you want to watch me play Fortnite?
I've got this cool new Star Wars skin.

02:06.000 --> 02:08.250
Well, I would, but, um…

02:09.125 --> 02:11.040
I got a surprise for you.

02:11.041 --> 02:13.874
We're gonna take a trip.
You, me, and your grandmother.

02:13.875 --> 02:14.790
Where?

02:14.791 --> 02:17.708
If I told you, it wouldn't be a surprise,
would it?

02:18.208 --> 02:19.749
But I need you to pack, okay?

02:19.750 --> 02:21.207
Only what you really want to take,

02:21.208 --> 02:23.790
and anything else you need,
we'll buy when we get there.

02:23.791 --> 02:24.708
Wait.

02:25.833 --> 02:27.291
Are we moving again?

02:28.916 --> 02:29.833
We are.

02:30.333 --> 02:31.833
Are we ever coming back?

02:33.458 --> 02:35.166
Go ahead and start packing.

02:36.125 --> 02:37.624
David is innocent!

02:37.625 --> 02:41.457
His son is alive, and he's being held
by a man named Hayden Payne!

02:41.458 --> 02:44.499
- No, Hayden Payne has been helping you.
- No, he hasn't.

02:44.500 --> 02:47.499
He's been manipulating us
to keep us from the truth.

02:47.500 --> 02:49.040
He's about to leave town.

02:49.041 --> 02:51.624
He left me this cryptic voicemail earlier
saying goodbye.

02:51.625 --> 02:53.290
- Wait, he's gonna run?
- Yeah.

02:53.291 --> 02:57.375
And if he does, if he does,
we will never see Matthew again!

02:58.458 --> 03:00.625
I know how crazy this all sounds.

03:03.250 --> 03:05.875
That boy I found that night,
it's not Matthew.

03:07.833 --> 03:09.166
I know.

03:11.166 --> 03:12.833
I know it wasn't Matthew.

03:15.833 --> 03:17.749
It's a little boy named Martin Bischoff.

03:17.750 --> 03:20.708
He disappeared from a Swiss orphanage
owned by the Paynes.

03:31.875 --> 03:34.708
I took care of the detective,
and I cleaned up the scene.

03:35.583 --> 03:38.750
But it is only a matter of time
before the FBI come calling.

03:39.666 --> 03:40.874
We have to leave.

03:40.875 --> 03:43.582
This is not gonna end
just because you're on a beach somewhere.

03:43.583 --> 03:45.375
They're gonna reopen the case,

03:46.083 --> 03:49.874
and then you and Hayden will spend
the rest of your life on the run.

03:49.875 --> 03:51.874
What other choice do we have?

03:51.875 --> 03:55.166
People think Matthew Burroughs
might still be alive.

03:57.291 --> 03:58.541
What if he wasn't?

03:59.500 --> 04:00.582
What are you saying?

04:00.583 --> 04:04.874
I'm saying what if he died that night,
and his body was never found?

04:04.875 --> 04:06.749
Nothing to connect to you.

04:06.750 --> 04:08.083
No need to run.

04:09.791 --> 04:12.582
As far as the world is concerned,

04:12.583 --> 04:14.166
he is a Payne.

04:15.833 --> 04:18.374
He may be the last of the Paynes,

04:18.375 --> 04:20.250
and Hayden loves him.

04:21.666 --> 04:22.958
Am I clear?

04:34.791 --> 04:37.166
- What were you two talking about?
- How's Theo?

04:38.291 --> 04:39.250
He's good.

04:39.791 --> 04:41.208
He's in his room packing.

04:41.791 --> 04:44.000
- Did he see anything?
- No.

04:44.583 --> 04:47.000
Make sure he stays in his room
until we leave.

04:48.458 --> 04:49.375
Hayden.

04:54.458 --> 04:56.333
That detective knew everything.

04:57.000 --> 05:00.916
You did what you had to,
and what you needed to for your son.

05:05.000 --> 05:06.000
Yeah.

05:07.875 --> 05:09.915
Wait, if you knew the body wasn't Matthew,

05:09.916 --> 05:12.540
why aren't the FBI out
looking for my son right now?

05:12.541 --> 05:13.624
It's not that simple.

05:13.625 --> 05:17.457
What do you mean it's not that simple?
He's been kidnapped by a psychopath!

05:17.458 --> 05:20.374
I've been suspended, so without
any hard evidence, I'm on my own.

05:20.375 --> 05:22.582
Well, fine, there are
a dozen cops out there right now.

05:22.583 --> 05:24.415
- I'll just go and ask one of them.
- You can't do that.

05:24.416 --> 05:26.624
- Why not?
- 'Cause you said it, he's a psychopath.

05:26.625 --> 05:28.749
So if he's surrounded
by cops and he feels threatened,

05:28.750 --> 05:30.749
then who knows
what he might do to Matthew?

05:30.750 --> 05:32.999
The Payne estate is a half hour
outside the city.

05:33.000 --> 05:35.040
Even if we leave now,
we may not catch them.

05:35.041 --> 05:37.207
Okay, we gotta delay him.
We gotta get there before he leaves.

05:37.208 --> 05:38.625
How? How will we do that?

05:39.916 --> 05:41.250
After I was attacked,

05:42.125 --> 05:44.374
he tried to convince me
to leave the country with him.

05:44.375 --> 05:46.249
He's not gonna think
that you changed your mind.

05:46.250 --> 05:47.375
He will…

05:48.666 --> 05:50.666
if he thinks you've been arrested.

05:55.416 --> 05:57.458
Rachel, I'm glad you called.

05:58.083 --> 06:00.541
Didn't think I'd ever hear from you again.

06:01.166 --> 06:02.583
Sorry, what?

06:03.833 --> 06:06.500
Uh, yeah. Yeah, okay.

06:07.291 --> 06:08.416
I could do that.

06:10.125 --> 06:12.457
You think Ronald will care
that I'm stealing his car?

06:12.458 --> 06:14.791
I don't even know where he is right now.

06:15.708 --> 06:18.624
Oh, uh, about that, Ronald,
I actually had him arrested.

06:18.625 --> 06:19.582
What?

06:19.583 --> 06:21.333
I'll clear it up, don't worry.

06:22.333 --> 06:25.165
- Be right behind you. Be careful.
- I need you to put these on.

06:25.166 --> 06:27.208
If anybody stops us,
I've arrested you, got it?

06:29.750 --> 06:30.958
- David?
- Yeah?

06:33.625 --> 06:35.791
There's so much
I-I need to say to you, but…

06:37.625 --> 06:39.041
Yeah, you don't have to.

06:40.625 --> 06:42.083
It's the past.

06:43.250 --> 06:45.125
Bring our son home, okay?

06:45.875 --> 06:47.416
Whatever it takes.

06:47.916 --> 06:49.166
You bring him home.

06:57.000 --> 06:59.790
And in breaking news,
The Boston Globe is now reporting

06:59.791 --> 07:04.540
that escaped fugitive David Burroughs
has been apprehended by the Boston police.

07:04.541 --> 07:06.165
Holy shit, they caught him.

07:06.166 --> 07:08.582
- It doesn't mean anything.
- He's going back to prison.

07:08.583 --> 07:09.791
For how long?

07:10.750 --> 07:13.332
He will be exonerated eventually,

07:13.333 --> 07:15.832
and then he'll start
looking all over again.

07:15.833 --> 07:17.666
Only this time, as a free man.

07:19.208 --> 07:20.458
We have to leave.

07:24.791 --> 07:25.791
Rachel.

07:27.166 --> 07:28.000
Are you okay?

07:29.083 --> 07:31.790
- David's been arrested.
- I saw on the news. What happened?

07:31.791 --> 07:35.665
We broke into the hospital to find Heller,
and David was caught.

07:35.666 --> 07:38.165
I got away, but I have nowhere to go.

07:38.166 --> 07:39.708
I don't know what to do.

07:40.416 --> 07:43.791
Hayden, the worst part is Heller's gone,
and we have no way to find Matthew now.

07:44.375 --> 07:45.250
How can I help?

07:46.375 --> 07:48.665
You told me we could
leave together, right?

07:48.666 --> 07:50.582
If the offer still stands,

07:50.583 --> 07:52.041
I'm ready, Hayden.

07:52.541 --> 07:55.166
I'm at my mother's estate.
How quick can you get here?

07:55.750 --> 07:58.208
I was hoping you'd say that,
'cause I'm almost there.

07:58.791 --> 08:00.333
- See you soon.
- Okay.

08:02.416 --> 08:04.874
How stupid can you be?

08:04.875 --> 08:07.124
I don't understand
your obsession with this woman.

08:07.125 --> 08:08.374
I love her, Mother.

08:08.375 --> 08:12.415
Oh, darling boy, there's a difference
between love and obsession.

08:12.416 --> 08:14.290
She is going to be your downfall.

08:14.291 --> 08:16.541
Is that why you had Stephano
try and kill her?

08:17.291 --> 08:21.125
Someone has to make the hard choices,
and it's certainly not going to be you.

08:21.791 --> 08:23.041
If anybody goes near us--

08:27.333 --> 08:29.458
There is no happily ever after
on this one.

08:30.041 --> 08:33.125
You don't think
that she'll know her own nephew?

08:33.791 --> 08:36.957
This whole thing started
because she saw that photograph

08:36.958 --> 08:38.624
and knew it was Matthew Burroughs.

08:38.625 --> 08:40.416
Who's Matthew Burroughs?

08:41.625 --> 08:42.541
Theo.

08:44.916 --> 08:47.124
You know you're not supposed to eavesdrop.

08:47.125 --> 08:49.415
I'm sorry. I didn't mean to.

08:49.416 --> 08:52.957
It's okay, buddy. Your grandmother and I
were just talking about our trip.

08:52.958 --> 08:56.041
And I can't find Rhino,
and I want to take him with us.

08:56.625 --> 08:59.625
Oh, okay. Well, I'll tell you what.

09:00.333 --> 09:03.125
Go back upstairs,
and I'll be right up there to help you.

09:12.666 --> 09:14.125
When she arrives,

09:15.208 --> 09:17.291
tell her that you can't help her.

09:18.041 --> 09:20.625
And then you get her to leave.

10:02.875 --> 10:04.125
It's just a precaution.

10:04.750 --> 10:05.915
Smart.

10:05.916 --> 10:08.375
Yeah. Whoever's behind all this
knows that I've been helping you.

10:10.000 --> 10:12.040
Thank you for letting me come here.

10:12.041 --> 10:13.915
I didn't know where else to go.

10:13.916 --> 10:15.041
Yeah.

10:18.500 --> 10:19.375
What?

10:20.166 --> 10:22.832
I can't help you anymore, Rachel.

10:22.833 --> 10:24.790
I thought you wanted to leave together.

10:24.791 --> 10:26.000
I do.

10:26.583 --> 10:28.833
Then what's the problem?

10:33.000 --> 10:34.416
Your mother, of course.

10:36.250 --> 10:39.416
I'm just confused because I thought
you said you wanted to protect me.

10:42.500 --> 10:43.958
And I need you.

10:45.083 --> 10:46.833
Right now more than ever.

10:49.625 --> 10:52.166
You know the only time
I've ever felt really safe is with you.

10:53.250 --> 10:54.541
If we leave, we…

10:55.416 --> 10:56.708
we can't come back.

10:58.208 --> 11:00.207
There's nothing for me here.

11:00.208 --> 11:02.041
Hasn't been for a long time.

11:06.375 --> 11:08.333
I want a fresh start together.

11:11.166 --> 11:12.625
Do you want that?

11:21.000 --> 11:24.124
Just, uh, wait in the great room.

11:24.125 --> 11:25.040
Okay.

11:25.041 --> 11:27.082
I'm gonna use the ladies' room
before we go.

11:27.083 --> 11:28.875
- It's down the hall. You know where it is.
- Yeah.

11:41.583 --> 11:43.040
Thank you for helping me.

11:43.041 --> 11:46.457
Don't thank me.
I'm taking you in as soon as this is over.

11:46.458 --> 11:48.457
This is just a pit stop,
as far as I'm concerned.

11:48.458 --> 11:50.583
As long as I get Matthew back,
that's all that matters.

11:58.916 --> 12:00.082
It's my partner.

12:00.083 --> 12:03.041
And I'm guessing
he wouldn't approve of our pit stop.

12:04.208 --> 12:05.375
He would not.

12:06.625 --> 12:09.124
You've reached
Agent Sarah Greer, I'm not able to…

12:09.125 --> 12:12.332
Oh, damn it, Sarah,
will you answer the damn phone?

12:12.333 --> 12:14.624
That's it.

12:14.625 --> 12:15.916
I'm getting out of here.

12:17.166 --> 12:18.625
Ah! Ah!

12:24.458 --> 12:27.832
Hey, this is gonna sound crazy.
Um, my name's Cheryl.

12:27.833 --> 12:31.665
- I know who you are, Dr. Dreason.
- Your partner, Agent Greer. She just left.

12:31.666 --> 12:32.832
Left to go where?

12:32.833 --> 12:34.875
To find my son. And, uh…

12:36.500 --> 12:37.624
David's with her.

12:37.625 --> 12:39.415
So he wasn't arrested.

12:39.416 --> 12:41.249
- No.
- You know where they're headed?

12:41.250 --> 12:42.207
The Payne estate.

12:42.208 --> 12:45.165
Hayden Payne was behind everything
that happened that night.

12:45.166 --> 12:48.583
Now, she said the FBI
couldn't do anything without proof.

12:49.833 --> 12:50.666
I have proof.

12:51.416 --> 12:54.208
Philip Mackenzie ran a DNA test for me.

12:54.791 --> 12:57.957
That proves the blood found
that night wasn't Matthew's.

12:57.958 --> 13:01.625
Which means the DNA results
used at the trial were doctored.

13:02.625 --> 13:03.958
David's innocent.

13:04.583 --> 13:07.083
My son is alive. Please.

13:07.958 --> 13:09.500
I need your help.

13:29.916 --> 13:31.665
- I thought I made myself clear.
- You did.

13:31.666 --> 13:34.457
- Then why is she still here?
- I can make this work.

13:34.458 --> 13:36.958
Hayden, she doesn't love you.

13:38.125 --> 13:39.582
We have a problem.

13:39.583 --> 13:40.957
No kidding.

13:40.958 --> 13:42.999
David Burroughs was never arrested.

13:43.000 --> 13:43.999
What?

13:44.000 --> 13:47.165
He's not in BPD or FBI custody.

13:47.166 --> 13:51.166
No one knows why The Globe ran that story
or who the source was.

13:55.291 --> 13:56.207
Rachel.

13:56.208 --> 13:58.290
You still think you can make this work?

13:58.291 --> 14:00.583
Burroughs is probably on his way here.

14:01.291 --> 14:02.625
What do you want to do?

14:05.291 --> 14:06.333
Let him come.

14:07.958 --> 14:09.333
She did us a favor.

14:09.916 --> 14:13.915
No one will question the killing
of two dangerous fugitives

14:13.916 --> 14:16.124
who've trespassed on private property.

14:16.125 --> 14:18.166
And I assume you finally agree.

14:54.416 --> 14:55.415
Get back in the car.

14:55.416 --> 14:56.583
I'm coming with you.

14:57.833 --> 15:00.124
You're still a fugitive, all right?
I said I'd help you.

15:00.125 --> 15:02.208
- We're not teaming up.
- You're right, we're not.

15:03.666 --> 15:05.374
I came out here on my own.
You followed me.

15:05.375 --> 15:08.416
And then when I get my son back,
you can arrest me and take me to jail.

15:12.875 --> 15:13.875
It's Rachel.

15:14.625 --> 15:16.541
There's armed guards at the house.

15:19.666 --> 15:22.750
I can help you. Now just let me--
Let me find him, please.

15:31.750 --> 15:34.750
- You okay?
- Yeah, just a little overwhelmed.

15:36.208 --> 15:37.415
You're safe now.

15:37.416 --> 15:40.958
And the fact that you're here
tells me you finally want what I want.

15:43.000 --> 15:43.833
I do.

15:44.500 --> 15:45.791
- You do?
- I do.

15:56.416 --> 15:58.083
Whoa, what are you doing?

15:59.083 --> 16:00.125
Hayden.

16:04.375 --> 16:05.208
Hayden?

16:06.500 --> 16:10.499
- Please, let me explain.
- I would've done anything for you.

16:10.500 --> 16:13.083
Please, please, just listen to me.

16:13.666 --> 16:14.916
You lied to me.

16:21.666 --> 16:23.500
You broke my heart.

16:36.500 --> 16:37.665
How do we get in?

16:37.666 --> 16:38.749
Side entrance.

16:38.750 --> 16:39.916
I can cover you.

16:46.041 --> 16:49.124
I hope you've come to your senses
and decided to tell me where she is.

16:49.125 --> 16:50.041
Sure, Julie.

16:50.625 --> 16:53.499
She's on her way to the Payne estate
to arrest Hayden Payne

16:53.500 --> 16:54.957
for murder and kidnapping.

16:54.958 --> 16:56.040
She's suspended.

16:56.041 --> 16:58.749
She can't arrest anyone.
You need to stop her.

16:58.750 --> 16:59.958
Can't. Sorry.

17:00.541 --> 17:01.707
She's ghosting me.

17:01.708 --> 17:03.165
Do you think this is funny?

17:03.166 --> 17:06.874
If she arrests Hayden Payne without proof,
they will sue us into oblivion,

17:06.875 --> 17:10.540
and your daughter will be lucky
to work security at a roadside motel.

17:10.541 --> 17:12.499
Hey! I got proof.

17:12.500 --> 17:13.915
I have a DNA test that proves

17:13.916 --> 17:17.458
the little boy who was murdered
that night was not Matthew Burroughs.

17:18.041 --> 17:19.832
I withdrew that test.

17:19.833 --> 17:21.624
Oh, yeah. Sure you did.

17:21.625 --> 17:23.540
But lucky for Sarah,
there was somebody else

17:23.541 --> 17:26.165
who cared about actually solving the case.

17:26.166 --> 17:30.208
Cheryl Dreason conducted her own DNA test.

17:31.041 --> 17:34.624
The blood at the scene was not a match
for Matthew Burroughs.

17:34.625 --> 17:36.915
That doesn't prove
Hayden Payne kidnapped anyone.

17:36.916 --> 17:38.207
I don't give a shit!

17:38.208 --> 17:40.249
It proves David Burroughs
didn't kill his own son.

17:40.250 --> 17:42.415
And you would've known that
if you weren't so busy

17:42.416 --> 17:44.582
trying to interfere
with Agent Greer's case.

17:44.583 --> 17:46.582
Be a shame if that got out, wouldn't it?

17:46.583 --> 17:47.957
Is that a threat?

17:47.958 --> 17:50.000
Yes! And I got another one for you!

17:50.625 --> 17:54.915
You're gonna send every agent we got
out to the Payne estate right now,

17:54.916 --> 17:57.457
or Dr. Dreason is gonna call…
What's the guy's name?

17:57.458 --> 17:59.707
Jim Doherty, managing editor of The Globe.

17:59.708 --> 18:01.790
Jim Doherty. Managing… Did you hear that?

18:01.791 --> 18:03.625
So send them now!

18:06.041 --> 18:06.958
Go.

18:12.375 --> 18:13.208
Ah!

18:21.958 --> 18:23.583
I broke your heart?

18:24.333 --> 18:26.832
You destroyed my family
and then pretended to help us.

18:26.833 --> 18:28.082
Why would you do that?

18:28.083 --> 18:30.540
All I've ever wanted is to be with you.

18:30.541 --> 18:33.958
And then I find out you go to Berg
to start your own family.

18:34.750 --> 18:35.666
Only…

18:36.916 --> 18:38.833
It was supposed to be you.

18:39.458 --> 18:41.291
How did you even find out about that?

18:41.875 --> 18:43.374
My assistant.

18:43.375 --> 18:45.333
She used to be the office manager there.

18:46.375 --> 18:49.875
Before Heller left Berg,
he ensured that I would be the donor.

18:50.625 --> 18:51.749
This is insane.

18:51.750 --> 18:55.125
The whole point of any of this
was for us to have a child.

18:55.916 --> 18:59.207
And when I realized what happened,
that it was Cheryl who went to Berg,

18:59.208 --> 19:00.707
I had to put it out of my mind.

19:00.708 --> 19:05.541
But then you, you brought me to that
Fourth of July party. You remember?

19:07.541 --> 19:09.875
And when I saw him for the first time,

19:10.958 --> 19:12.625
I understood everything.

19:13.125 --> 19:15.958
I knew I was meant to be his father.

19:16.625 --> 19:20.291
And what about the little boy you killed
that night to take Matthew's place?

19:21.125 --> 19:22.124
What about him?

19:22.125 --> 19:25.291
He was gonna die a painful death
from his condition. It doesn't matter.

19:27.416 --> 19:28.708
Can you hear yourself?

19:31.125 --> 19:32.000
Can you?

19:32.916 --> 19:35.083
You're not well, Hayden.

19:37.250 --> 19:39.583
There is something deeply wrong with you.

19:40.250 --> 19:42.125
Well, now there it is.

19:43.166 --> 19:45.625
Now we know how you really feel about him.

19:46.208 --> 19:49.166
And for the record, I never did like you.

20:16.500 --> 20:17.750
Did you hear that?

20:18.500 --> 20:22.125
Well, it seems as if David Burroughs
has met his unfortunate end.

20:23.333 --> 20:24.790
You won't get away with it.

20:24.791 --> 20:26.500
Don't be so naive.

20:27.375 --> 20:29.250
Hayden, it's time to go.

20:33.750 --> 20:37.500
Everything I've done,
I've done to be with my son.

20:38.000 --> 20:40.125
And I am a good father, Rachel.
He loves me.

20:43.583 --> 20:45.166
He's not your son, Hayden.

20:46.250 --> 20:47.375
Of course he is.

20:49.666 --> 20:51.415
Cheryl was pregnant
before she went to Berg.

20:51.416 --> 20:52.582
Oh, please.

20:52.583 --> 20:54.374
Do a paternity test and you'll see.

20:54.375 --> 20:56.540
We did. And he's a Payne.

20:56.541 --> 20:58.500
Did you see the test, Hayden?

20:59.958 --> 21:02.625
- We don't have time for this. Come on.
- Did you?

21:11.791 --> 21:13.041
Is he mine?

21:14.083 --> 21:15.875
Can't you see what she's doing?

21:16.458 --> 21:18.041
He needs to know the truth.

21:22.291 --> 21:25.375
You told me he was my son.

21:26.708 --> 21:27.915
- Enough.
- Answer me.

21:27.916 --> 21:29.583
- Enough!
- Is he mine?

21:31.000 --> 21:32.958
Don't ask questions…

21:33.916 --> 21:35.875
that you don't want the answers to.

22:01.833 --> 22:03.291
Who are you?

22:29.750 --> 22:30.791
I'm David.

22:33.083 --> 22:34.250
What's going on?

22:36.458 --> 22:38.083
We're not here to hurt you.

22:39.458 --> 22:40.875
I know you're scared.

22:41.875 --> 22:43.625
I need you to come with us.

22:44.375 --> 22:45.375
Why?

22:52.708 --> 22:54.000
You still have Rhino.

22:55.541 --> 22:57.166
How do you know his name?

22:59.500 --> 23:01.291
Because I bought it for you.

23:02.875 --> 23:05.500
You wouldn't remember
because you were three.

23:13.833 --> 23:16.250
Your actual name is Matthew Burroughs.

23:18.666 --> 23:20.083
And I'm your father.

23:24.583 --> 23:26.332
We're gonna take you someplace safe, okay?

23:26.333 --> 23:29.000
I know you're really scared,
but we need to go right now.

23:32.166 --> 23:33.125
Come on.

23:35.583 --> 23:38.040
You said he was my son.

23:38.041 --> 23:39.708
What did you expect me to do?

23:40.291 --> 23:43.874
There was no going back
after what you did that night.

23:43.875 --> 23:45.875
So I told you what you wanted to hear.

23:46.458 --> 23:49.833
When I got the results,
I made sure you would never find out.

23:51.125 --> 23:54.874
He is the one person who truly loves me!

23:54.875 --> 23:55.874
And he still does.

23:55.875 --> 23:58.749
I'm a good father, and it's the only thing
I've ever been good at!

23:58.750 --> 24:01.332
Hayden, listen to me. Nothing has changed.

24:01.333 --> 24:03.541
Everything has changed!

24:04.125 --> 24:08.166
I have nothing now!
You have taken everything from me!

24:08.750 --> 24:10.540
Oh, that is rich!

24:10.541 --> 24:13.125
I have given you everything!

24:13.875 --> 24:17.290
You were born into status and privilege.

24:17.291 --> 24:18.790
And what did you do with it?

24:18.791 --> 24:23.082
You have brought this family's legacy
to the brink of extinction.

24:23.083 --> 24:26.875
I am not going to allow you
to be a cautionary tale.

24:27.916 --> 24:29.250
You're weak.

24:30.458 --> 24:33.416
Hayden, you've always been weak.

24:34.000 --> 24:35.458
But it's okay.

24:36.041 --> 24:37.583
Because I love you.

24:38.458 --> 24:39.666
And you have me.

24:41.250 --> 24:42.833
You'll always have me.

24:44.708 --> 24:45.833
Ah!

25:03.333 --> 25:06.915
Hold on. Hold on. Take him to the car.
I have to go back for Rachel.

25:06.916 --> 25:08.625
You go with her, all right?
You're gonna be safe, I promise.

25:12.833 --> 25:14.333
You're not taking my son!

25:14.916 --> 25:17.290
Give Theo back, or Rachel dies.

25:17.291 --> 25:19.790
- You don't have to do this, please.
- Lower your weapon.

25:19.791 --> 25:20.832
Not gonna happen.

25:20.833 --> 25:22.582
Put it down now, or she's dead!

25:22.583 --> 25:24.165
Let her go!

25:24.166 --> 25:25.457
Last warning, Hayden!

25:25.458 --> 25:27.458
Give me back my son!

25:30.750 --> 25:32.374
- Dad?
- It's okay, buddy.

25:32.375 --> 25:34.291
Don't hurt her, please.

25:35.791 --> 25:36.832
I'll go with you.

25:36.833 --> 25:38.291
No, Matthew.

25:39.916 --> 25:40.833
No!

25:42.333 --> 25:43.499
Don't hurt him, I'm begging you.

25:43.500 --> 25:45.541
- Don't be stupid, Hayden!
- Stop!

25:46.958 --> 25:47.916
Let him go!

26:12.833 --> 26:13.916
Theo!

26:28.333 --> 26:29.666
Theo?

26:31.833 --> 26:33.291
Where are you, buddy?

26:37.916 --> 26:41.083
Those people, they--
They want to take you away!

26:43.541 --> 26:46.874
Whatever they told you, it isn't true!

26:46.875 --> 26:48.541
We're family, you and me!

26:49.125 --> 26:51.000
I love you. You know that!

26:51.750 --> 26:52.875
Oh!

27:10.958 --> 27:11.791
David!

27:12.583 --> 27:14.291
Drop the gun. Drop it now!

27:21.500 --> 27:24.000
All I ever wanted was a family of my own.

27:24.833 --> 27:26.583
You can still do the right thing.

27:27.458 --> 27:28.375
Just let him go.

27:36.166 --> 27:38.500
You're the best thing
that ever happened to me.

27:46.666 --> 27:47.708
No!

27:52.083 --> 27:52.916
David.

27:57.000 --> 28:00.375
I'm right here. Stay with me, come on.
Come on, I'm right here.

28:06.166 --> 28:07.541
I found you.

28:11.125 --> 28:12.999
I'm right here, all right?

28:13.000 --> 28:14.874
Stay with me. Come on.

28:14.875 --> 28:16.041
David.

28:29.791 --> 28:31.874
My name is David Burroughs.

28:31.875 --> 28:35.624
I served five years of a life sentence
for killing my son.

28:35.625 --> 28:38.166
Until I broke out of prison to rescue him.

28:38.750 --> 28:41.125
If you're from Boston,
you might've read about it.

28:42.291 --> 28:43.958
If you're not, you will soon.

28:44.750 --> 28:46.249
Within weeks of saving Matthew,

28:46.250 --> 28:48.790
my conviction was overturned
and I was freed.

28:48.791 --> 28:52.082
But I wasn't the only one who was given
the blessing of a new beginning.

28:52.083 --> 28:54.541
Cheryl gave birth to a baby girl.

28:55.500 --> 28:57.915
And after what Ronald did
to help us find Matthew,

28:57.916 --> 29:00.125
he and Cheryl found their way
back to each other.

29:01.041 --> 29:03.415
But not all new beginnings are planned.

29:03.416 --> 29:06.665
Some are born of necessity
and even consequence.

29:06.666 --> 29:08.999
Adam lost his shield
for helping me escape.

29:09.000 --> 29:12.082
The upside was Nicky
had no use for him as a civilian.

29:12.083 --> 29:15.124
He works as a PI now
with another former cop from the BPD.

29:15.125 --> 29:17.665
Did you invoice the wife
on that babysitter case?

29:17.666 --> 29:20.540
Yeah, I will.
As soon as you stop busting my balls.

29:20.541 --> 29:21.582
What balls?

29:21.583 --> 29:24.832
I'm not sure if we'll ever
be the brothers we once were.

29:24.833 --> 29:27.791
But I do know without his help,
I wouldn't be here.

29:28.583 --> 29:31.791
I wouldn't be here
without the help of a lot of people.

29:32.583 --> 29:34.374
Agent Greer took over for her dad

29:34.375 --> 29:37.750
as head of the Boston Fugitive Task Force
when Max retired.

29:39.375 --> 29:40.790
Or at least tried to retire.

29:40.791 --> 29:43.165
- What are you doing here?
- I just came by.

29:43.166 --> 29:45.124
Thought maybe you might
want to go to lunch.

29:45.125 --> 29:49.332
Well, I'm sorry.
I'm actually really swamped in a case.

29:49.333 --> 29:51.000
Oh, well, is, um…

29:51.916 --> 29:53.833
What, you got something that, uh…

29:54.875 --> 29:57.125
maybe you need another set of eyes on?

30:08.916 --> 30:11.499
My father passed away
less than a week ago.

30:11.500 --> 30:14.083
But not before getting to spend
several months with his grandson,

30:14.750 --> 30:18.833
instilling as much information about
the Boston Red Sox as humanly possible.

30:30.375 --> 30:31.540
Sorry.

30:31.541 --> 30:33.333
I'll go back inside soon.

30:35.250 --> 30:36.375
It's okay.

30:42.708 --> 30:45.458
Sometimes with a lot of people,
I just get…

30:46.541 --> 30:47.666
I don't know.

30:49.250 --> 30:50.416
Yeah, me too.

30:51.833 --> 30:53.582
Before Lenny died,

30:53.583 --> 30:57.750
he told me a story about a barbecue
I was at on the Fourth of July.

30:58.791 --> 31:00.208
Yeah, that was his favorite holiday.

31:01.125 --> 31:03.708
I told him I remembered
because he was sick.

31:05.000 --> 31:06.041
But I didn't.

31:07.583 --> 31:08.708
I want to.

31:10.666 --> 31:12.250
What if I never do?

31:13.375 --> 31:16.041
Great thing about memories
is you can make more of them.

31:18.083 --> 31:20.708
It's just people don't appreciate
how special they are.

31:24.291 --> 31:25.458
But you will.

31:27.958 --> 31:29.000
Yeah.

31:31.666 --> 31:35.415
What Matthew's been through,
few people can understand.

31:35.416 --> 31:37.540
Luckily, I'm one of them.

31:37.541 --> 31:40.540
Our shared struggle back to the life
we were supposed to have

31:40.541 --> 31:43.707
has bonded us in both heartbreak and hope.

31:43.708 --> 31:46.082
- There he is.
- Hello.

31:46.083 --> 31:48.250
Let me go

31:49.666 --> 31:53.625
I don't wanna be your hero

31:55.000 --> 31:58.333
I don't wanna be a big man

31:59.083 --> 32:01.916
Just wanna fight with everyone else

32:02.875 --> 32:04.415
Lenny would have loved this.

32:04.416 --> 32:06.125
Your masquerade

32:06.958 --> 32:08.415
Everybody here together.

32:08.416 --> 32:10.332
I don't wanna be a part…

32:10.333 --> 32:12.250
Yeah, assuming the game wasn't on.

32:12.833 --> 32:13.916
Obviously.

32:15.125 --> 32:17.582
I know the road ahead isn't gonna be easy.

32:17.583 --> 32:19.749
Nothing worth fighting for ever is.

32:19.750 --> 32:22.457
What I do know
is when it comes to Matthew,

32:22.458 --> 32:26.290
wherever that road leads,
however dangerous or mundane,

32:26.291 --> 32:29.125
I'll be by his side every step of the way.

32:29.708 --> 32:32.040
And if he ever strays or gets lost
and needs my help,

32:32.041 --> 32:34.499
I'll find him and bring him back.

32:34.500 --> 32:36.874
A night out on the weekend

32:36.875 --> 32:38.708
I'll always find him.

32:39.458 --> 32:42.708
And we can whisper things

32:43.625 --> 32:48.291
Secrets from our American dreams

32:50.500 --> 32:54.041
Baby needs some protection

32:54.833 --> 32:57.666
But I'm a kid like everyone else

33:01.791 --> 33:04.541
So let me go

33:05.583 --> 33:09.875
I don't wanna be your hero

33:11.041 --> 33:14.458
I don't wanna be a big man

33:15.083 --> 33:18.125
I just wanna fight like everyone else

33:44.041 --> 33:46.833
So let me go

33:47.958 --> 33:52.416
I don't wanna be your hero

33:53.583 --> 33:57.125
I don't wanna be a big man

33:57.708 --> 34:00.625
I just wanna fight with everyone else

34:02.166 --> 34:05.333
Your masquerade

34:05.958 --> 34:10.166
I don't wanna be a part of your parade

34:11.416 --> 34:14.916
Everyone deserves a chance to

34:16.000 --> 34:18.625
Walk with everyone else
